# Settings of the agent (`python -m d2c.agent` and the runs started from the web view).
# Copy to .env and uncomment one variant. Values in <angle brackets> are placeholders.
# Write comments on their own lines: an env file does not strip them behind a value.

# 1. Claude login: no key. On a host the agent uses the login of Claude Code on that machine.
# In a container, give it a token from `claude setup-token`.
# D2C_LLM_MODEL=sonnet
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=<token from claude setup-token>

# 2. Anthropic API key
# D2C_LLM_API_KEY=<anthropic api key>
# D2C_LLM_MODEL=sonnet

# 3. OpenRouter (Anthropic models; the URL has no /v1)
# D2C_LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
# D2C_LLM_API_KEY=<openrouter api key>
# D2C_LLM_MODEL=anthropic/<model>

# 4. Ollama on the host. From a container use http://host.docker.internal:11434.
# The model needs tool support and the server a context of 64000 tokens or more: OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=64000 ollama serve
# D2C_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# D2C_LLM_MODEL=<model from ollama list>

# Optional for every variant.
# A second model builds the part from the spec; the first one only reads the drawing.
# D2C_LLM_BUILD_MODEL=<model>
# The MCP server: stdio (default), a URL such as http://mcp:8765/mcp, or a command line.
# D2C_MCP_URL=docker run -i --rm --network none -v <drawings folder>:/data:ro -v <results folder>:/app/results d2c
